phases.prompt:
Score this release candidate's readiness from 0 to 1 and explain why. End your reply with a line in the form: score: <number>

CANDIDATE:
${input}

code.source:
const m = String(input).match(/score\s*[:=]?\s*([0-9]*\.?[0-9]+)/i);
const s = m ? parseFloat(m[1]) : 0;
return s >= 0.8 ? 'ship' : s >= 0.5 ? 'hold' : 'block';

ship.prompt:
Readiness cleared the bar — roll out the candidate.

EVAL:
${eval}

hold.prompt:
Borderline readiness — list the few must-fix items before we re-evaluate.

EVAL:
${eval}

default.prompt:
Not ready to ship — identify the blocking risks and the safest next step.

EVAL:
${eval}
